  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia-Australia Comprehensive Economic Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment, which is also known as KATALIS, supports Indonesia-Australia Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (IA-CEPA) which was entered into force on 5 July 2020. KATALIS aims at a more comprehensive, high quality and mutually beneficial economic partnership between Indonesia and Australia, which covers trade in goods (including non-tariff measures, rules of origin, customs procedures, trade facilitation, sanitary and phytosanitary, technical barrier to trade), trade in services (including professional services, financial services, telecommunication services, and movement of natural persons), electronic commerce, investment, economic cooperation, competition, and legal provision.</narrative>
  </description>
